   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 35pt;"><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">Accounts Receivable</span></p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 35pt;">The Company records accounts receivables due from dealers/distributors, large end-users such as retail stores, security companies and law enforcement agencies.&#160;Accounts receivable, net of allowances, was $<ix:nonFraction id="c139408375" contextRef="i_2025-11-30" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:AccountsReceivableNetCurrent" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">10.8</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million, $<ix:nonFraction id="c139408376" contextRef="i_2024-11-30" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:AccountsReceivableNetCurrent" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">2.6</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million, and $<ix:nonFraction id="c139408377" contextRef="i_2023-11-30" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:AccountsReceivableNetCurrent" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">2.9</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million&#160;as of&#160;<em style="font: inherit;"> November 30, 2025, </em><em style="font: inherit;">2024</em> and <em style="font: inherit;">2023</em>&#160;respectively.&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;&#160;</p>
