   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 35pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 35pt;">The trademarks have an&#160;indefinite life and will be assessed annually for impairment.&#160; All other intangible assets are finite-lived.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 35pt;">Intangible assets amortization&#160;expenses are recorded within operating expenses in the accompanying Consolidated Statements of Operations and Comprehensive Income.&#160; Total intangible assets amortization expense&#160;for the years ended&#160;<em style="font: inherit;"> November 30, 2025 </em>and <em style="font: inherit;">2024</em>&#160;were&#160;$<ix:nonFraction id="c139408403" contextRef="d_2024-12-01_2025-11-30" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfIntangibleAssets" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">0.3</ix:nonFraction>  million&#160;and&#160;$<ix:nonFraction id="c139408404" contextRef="d_2023-12-01_2024-11-30" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfIntangibleAssets" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">0.3</ix:nonFraction>  million, respectively.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 35pt;">Estimated future amortization expense related to intangible assets&#160;as of <em style="font: inherit;"> November 30, 2025</em>, are as follows (in thousands):</p>
